2eba8b5440f42eddc12015a003e558ea26fd512cf1827a7a3.png) ![](images/54/54827258e24002d07ac1bc4468c8a8f81fa9ee932f102790093989c200860788.png) and ![](images/1b/1b0eaf7c23571a3806b1fdbcb5badeb8127cefe1f5d71ea8d1ea426aa2e0fbff.png)" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234981 1072 #uuid "4031c8a9-0559-5d8d-a1a5-6e3402c19b27" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234981 1074 "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the ![](images/33/3397de904d08c80f853cc9ad930c0792c5f6033aa1409655c4623fe3a0edfc86.png)-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n![](images/de/de82f740c53922156a55045b891d73187af742855d8687380f2147468b6625a4.png)\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the ![](images/b7/b7058c5c6e450acdb37c5e67a76139fe8c17abcc4003b200af69d62540050db9.png)-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n![](images/08/081a487a9615ca41e08647729d379a07b4c63e856d8db5d20357ee6e379f9e56.png)\nwhere ![](images/59/5990121d9274012f291f6d3622d0ba077bd009023969faa36b1058d05f4e1962.png) is the interior of the circle ![](images/ea/eab35e9389dfcc153b3ff22e36ff359595c386b3733d61589a04807c25bc56cf.png)\n\nAs a result, the volume of ![](images/e7/e72f4ff500bcbe3f2392425e3b4b777888f579ae6ece9546ca0dae0c08c33493.png) is given by\n![](images/2d/2d850bd7a9cc12a8143f7ee1a9803e4d6ea98ae1c22cfc56e1c5ce989b512f94.png)\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of ![](images/83/837e84cb3633847bb8928cfb823f7c20756bd92362517e5411a0e77684da47a8.png) consists of\n\n- the lower part ![](images/5e/5e020d44aa4de1a4a3c561677f7b0a46ffc9a6b5f1a670fdb4d6ec93f837bf15.png) and\n\n- the upper part ![](images/67/674107266131d1e4e7e3b7147c7eab59e380cbb30c04c44f8942b0ea688973ac.png)\n\nfor ![](images/54/542abe7b3c7cdba70586108ad546acee635ad90d16326b8bad3f7ba430de3f08.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n![](images/3c/3c8cf015e3b1944ce18fa83f77a17912afc696e485dc6557760a1d78bfd81e3c.png)\n\nSo,\n![](images/1b/1bc658f161ad3523eaf0a263af0a9b86