ce,\n![](images/da/da5024a9515dce187468fd87b63acfd0fd89bfd867a9f03388782221604a3e74.png)\n\nSimilarly,\n\n- ![](images/cb/cb4b9bd2f50fd4b2da78369b90c522bc2b7ee20cbafa9460b643889733487c5b.png)\n\n- ![](images/5f/5fdd95564252a9a4218055ca7670a535233aa026955b7e410700e26c4f7d170c.png) and ![](images/1f/1f42d4df263db3845ca2361b8f89c4075e0cdb9b39e5564c39ae82115932a201.png) have opposite directions\n\nHence,\n![](images/da/da69cf085ea0816397356abf0878c798ab653c04fe34a51b8b849610d57778d4.png)\n\nAdditionally,\n\n![](images/57/5765a85c90552570f9a2a041f2f324a9fa0ce183d42708344531a13fbee802c8.png)\n\nConsequently,\n![](images/57/578802d62c9ab4cfbc8f250975b5b7be1396907593ba95901b8b21ad6a116d04.png)\n\nSince ![](images/46/466863f8c7522ac89896a4233a823be02940535097c28328fa2c9e9e1f4bc3d8.png) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](images/37/3720c5887713d3f7a29be384fe5e883390935b2b9b469af626a8dba968f4da8b.png) we get\n\n![](images/1c/1c2480355dc4e29a136a3bd7b6855e076f1c9698507523cafbd934521b91c6bf.png)" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234983 1069 "e-40653" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234983 1071 "Which of the following functions are piecewise smooth on ![](images/11/1146bea1d20a4478e32e2d6c1000dc43dc14ae8a592660fc7618792c8231c671.png)\n![](images/c0/c07d756afce881fc79fc5da71aa8fb12a913a6ae244971b6519b9cd6b3c1a9a9.png)" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234983 1072 #uuid "c708cbd0-1811-5856-a1f9-ef9054cde811" 13194139533384 17592186045585 true] [17592186234983 1074 "A function ![](images/12/12a2b198bc9d42170a9aeb3d0390ccee0463bab7c637bf4a4642750332aeeba0.png) is **piecewise smooth** on ![](images/ba/ba299c06d373f7efc4870693613b428130d4aaa58dc9b4736a10934bd5c13dc8.png) if\n\n- ![](images/a6/a600da93d54ed8b4857befa58c1165e8c02b77d1c2fc5b1f460961dc135c50a7.png) is piecewise continuous on ![](images/2e/2e98ef221b52709cba639943b3948fcc9596a64c5fa9ad4753f52fba8d3381c1.png) and\n\n- ![](images/98/982f4